00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.669
And then also compositing with composer

60
00:02:54.669 --> 00:02:57.550
and practical lighting capabilities

61
00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.469
and being able to control lights through DMX.

62
00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:04.590
Now, these key virtual production technologies,

63
00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.810
there's some in specific that I wanna call out.

64
00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.509
First are a series of production design tools.

65
00:03:10.509 --> 00:03:15.240
So production design is unquestionably

66
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.639
one of the most important aspects

67
00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:21.860
of the whole LED volume in-camera visual effects process.

68
00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:26.139
You need to be able to adequately create

69
00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.560
and prepare the items that you plan to shoot,

70
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.860
whether it's practically or virtually.

71
00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.020
So in a virtual setting, we wanna talk about

72
00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.099
being able to do virtual set scouting.

73
00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:43.580
We wanna be able to combine various GIS data,

74
00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.520
LIDAR data, drone scanning, and so forth

75
00:03:46.539 --> 00:03:49.860
in order to create the worlds that you plan to shoot.

76
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.180
And this can be very important

77
00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.139
when you're trying to decide

78
00:03:54.139 --> 00:03:56.379
how much needs to be practically shot

79
00:03:56.379 --> 00:03:59.560
versus how much can be done inside of an LED wall.

80
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.659
And when you have these environments scanned and built,

81
00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:07.699
they can be really crucial, critical even,

82
00:04:07.699 --> 00:04:10.219
for your planning process in pre-production.

83
00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:11.699
How great would it be to be able

84
00:04:11.699 --> 00:04:13.939
to basically have a scan of the environment

85
00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:16.139
of where you're planning to eventually shoot

86
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:17.920
live action elements in?

87
00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.040
From there, you can set scout

88
00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:24.670
and look at all of the different options available to you.

89
00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.389
There's also some key virtual production technologies

90
00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:29.509
for various visualization tools.

91
00:04:29.509 --> 00:04:32.509
Now, I talked about previs.

92
00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:34.610
Previs was a very early forerunner

93
00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.829
to a lot of the processes and workflows

94
00:04:36.829 --> 00:04:39.389
that we're utilizing and observing

95
00:04:39.389 --> 00:04:41.790
in the ICV effects process.

96
00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.389
But now with real-time previs,

97
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.810
you have the option of basically being more iterative

98
00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:51.129
and having the ability to interact with the data

99
00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:54.529
and have potentially your director,

100
00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:57.970
your visual effects supervisor, your cinematographer,

101
00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:00.810
all being able to come in and look at Unreal

102
00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.490
in order to provide their feedback in real time.

103
00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.089
You can do character blocking,

104
00:05:05.089 --> 00:05:07.290
you can do virtual camera blocking,

105
00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.949
and all of this can be either done on the day

106
00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.529
or potentially, again,

107
00:05:12.529 --> 00:05:15.810
using the multi-user capabilities inside of Unreal,

108
00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.910
you could potentially have the ability for your director,

109
00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.930
your cinematographer, your motion capture actors,

110
00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.649
all in different locations,

111
00:05:25.649 --> 00:05:29.129
working together in session within Unreal Engine.

112
00:05:29.129 --> 00:05:31.649
This will, again, ultimately feed the whole ability

113
00:05:31.649 --> 00:05:35.209
to create some really nice preliminary sequence designs

114
00:05:35.209 --> 00:05:36.069
and constructions,

115
00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:39.069
which can feed the whole creative process.
